From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: starfive: fix PineTab-V camera startup and stream lifetime

The async framework completes only the root notifier. Select video-mux's
firmware default when the matching sensor binds, then initialize the entire
enabled pipeline from the sensor in the CAMSS root completion callback.
Initialize capture sizes from their actual source formats as well.

Linux 7.3 CSI2RX uses the stream-aware API. Call its helpers with
the firmware-selected source pad for both raw and ISP capture so either
PineTab-V sensor can start through the mux with the selected lane map.

Program raw DMA addresses before enabling the writer, stop DMA and drain
interrupt handlers before returning buffers, and unwind capture startup if
the source fails. Reapply the startup frame skip on every capture. Match
NV12 buffer stride and chroma alignment to the ISP hardware. Bound GC02M2
blanking controls to its 14-bit timing registers and reject active format
changes during capture.

The board GPIOs and lane maps are unchanged; they match the PineTab-V
revision-1 and revision-2 camera switch wiring.

Link: https://files.pine64.org/doc/PineTab/PineTab-V_Schematic_Ver2-20240730.pdf
Link: https://docs.kernel.org/driver-api/media/v4l2-async.html
Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI)
---

